# Environment variables

## Vercel (already provided by Prisma / Postgres integration)

These are managed by the integration (no Edit) — that is fine:

| Key | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| `DATABASE_URL` | Used by Prisma (keep as-is from integration) |
| `PRISMA_DATABASE_URL` | Integration helper |
| `POSTGRES_URL` | Direct Postgres URL |

**Also add manually:**

| Key | Value |
|-----|--------|
| `JWT_SECRET` | long random string (e.g. `acme-salary-management-system-super-secure-production-key-2024`) |

## Local (.env)

For local dev against the same Postgres (recommended for this project):

```bash
npx vercel env pull .env
```

Or set:

```env
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..."   # paste from Vercel → Copy DATABASE_URL / POSTGRES_URL
JWT_SECRET="your-long-random-secret"
```

Do **not** use `file:./dev.db` anymore — the app uses PostgreSQL.
